= Exporting as PDF <sec-export>

The finished document comes from the export: project menu, "Export as PDF …" (Shift+Cmd+E). The dialog shows the templates as small pictures on the left, their settings in the middle and a preview of the pages on the right, which updates when you change something. A template decides everything that belongs to the look: paper, margins, typefaces, headings, quotations, tables, headers and footers.

Six templates come with the program: Monograph, Journal, Margin notes, Manuscript, Essay and Report. Pick one, look at the preview and switch. From a template you can make a copy of your own and change it element by element, from the body text to the page number.

== Title page and front matter <sec-titlepage>

The title page prints what is in the front matter: title, subtitle, authors with their institution, date and version. The dedication, the abstract and the preface stand before the table of contents. If an author is missing, the export tells you beforehand.

== What is still open <sec-still-open>

Before saving, the dialog names what is still open: comments, missing citations and citations to check, references to nowhere and pictures that are still missing. Each line leads to the place. So none of it ends up unnoticed in a submission.
